{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_16-30-57-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A1: A client proposal is batched by its receiving replica into a local-row instance. Conflict indexes supply sequence/dependencies; thriftiness selects a preferred live peer subset. PreAccept replies are filtered by attempted ballot and phase, then counted/merged. Fast conditions commit directly; otherwise Accept replies at matching ballot establish the coordinator commit threshold. Commit broadcasts carry commands and attributes. Recipients install guarded committed records. Dependency/SCC execution waits for prerequisite commands and committed status, applies ordered operations and answers deferred clients.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-form\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-execute\",\n        \"B-client\",\n        \"B-config\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-phase1\",\n        \"M-accept\",\n        \"M-send\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-exec\",\n        \"M-replica\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A2: Authority is per instance, not exclusive global proposal leadership. Initial ballots equal origin replica ID. Recovery resets bookkeeping while retaining client proposals/value context, selects a ballot, adds a self reply and sends Prepare. Acceptors raise their promise and export prior value ballot/status. The recovering coordinator collects matching replies and selects a highest-value-ballot tuple before committing locally, accepting or restarting phase1. Lower-ballot requests and nonmatching replies are guarded. Complete committed records skip recovery. Master designation affects higher-ballot retry but does not stop other replicas proposing.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-recover-trigger\",\n        \"B-config\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-recovery\",\n        \"M-ballot\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-master\",\n        \"M-dispatch\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A1/A2 connection: The record status and value ballot exported by Prepare determine whether earlier formation support constrains the new attempt as committed, accepted or merely preaccepted. Reset bookkeeping discards old counts; phase and ballot checks constrain delayed replies. Accepted/committed follower guards limit new PreAccept modifications, while delayed Commit is rejected below a newer promise. Pending local client proposals survive recovery and may be reproposed after NOOP. Execution later consumes the selected record, so retention of support classification matters independently of client visibility.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-form\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-execute\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-record\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-phase1\",\n        \"M-accept\",\n        \"M-recovery\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-exec\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Follower Accept leaves Status unchanged; investigate preservation through Prepare.\",\n      \"Prepare selection overwrites equal-VBallot tuples in reply order; recoverer also rewrites self vbal before exporting it.\",\n      \"TryPreAccept recovery subcase has duplicate condition after the prior branch; deeper reachability remains open.\",\n      \"Transport queues per message asynchronously; legal dispatch histories and shared-memory observations need question-specific review.\",\n      \"Fault/restart and client retry contracts remain incomplete.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation, authority transition, old-work guards and consumption are traced with source-backed unresolved local discrepancies; no correctness or coverage claim.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"978eea8f2dd048948021ef642fa75c01\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"978eea8f2dd048948021ef642fa75c01\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"67ded6