t, quorum thresholds and thriftiness.\",\n          \"B-execute\": \"Explains consequence of a subsequently committed tuple.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"preservation\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"Follower Accept rejects lower ballots and protects committed records.\",\n          \"Accept does update bal, vbal, Seq and Deps; retaining these could supply protection independent of Status.\",\n          \"Coordinator sets its own ACCEPTED status before broadcasting Accept; recovery may obtain that record.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Which legal quorum history can lose coordinator evidence while retaining follower acknowledgements?\",\n          \"Does subsequent value-ballot selection independently preserve the accepted tuple despite the status discrepancy?\",\n          \"What narrow responsibility is grounded by the producer/consumer contract without assuming a whole-cluster violation?\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 0,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Source discrepancy is between acknowledged follower writes and the recovery consumer that explicitly distinguishes ACCEPTED from PREACCEPTED/NONE. Trace a legal prefix and selection before committing to a formal test; smaller source work can distinguish alternative protection.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Register the initial connected implementation map and investigate a sourced support-retention discrepancy without asserting a violation.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null,\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"67ded68bdd3b49d7ba28b333d9eb0caf\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\"