{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md; cat ../agent-source/dlog/dlog.go; sed -n '1,63p' ../agent-source/replica/replica.go; cat ../agent-source/rpc/rpc.go; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'));print(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['ExploreSubmission'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md; cat ../agent-source/dlog/dlog.go; sed -n '1,63p' ../agent-source/replica/replica.go; cat ../agent-source/rpc/rpc.go; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'));print(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['ExploreSubmission'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"SEMANTIC REVIEW Use the supplied contract against fixed inputs, source dependencies and observations. One checker_correspondence review covers requirement versus encoded predicate, entry/caller duties, oracle, identity, legal history, observation path/completion and counterevidence. Use experiments.md for these criteria, including wait/cleanup ownership and finite progress observations; unexamined continuation triggers remain gaps under the stated scheduling assumptions. Applicability and decomposition need separate answers only for concrete issues. No issue found is provisional, not proof or an independent vote.\n\nCURRENT VERSION Cite unchanged established parts and focus on the increment: what changed, which premise it answers, what the new execution observed and what remains unanswered. Verify that the fixed entry, prefix and schedule still exercise the original discriminator: stronger setup must not exclude the investigated premise. A narrower scope cannot settle its parent; substantive changes use the existing revision rules. New inputs require fresh execution and correspondence; old review success cannot certify them. Scope/cause/consequence questions outside the checked proposition are independent limits, not additional confirmation gates. Never alter a requirement or weaken a predicate merely to obtain a passing test.\n\nISSUES Fixed Claim, Harness and Monitor conflicts have exact issue/condition records. Address the listed issue with a sourced resolution and, where supplied, condition dispositions; do not answer the same conflict separately in several products. A no_issue_found item alone clears nothing. Preserve current counterevidence as an open issue, explained alternatives in rationale and independent limits in limitations. Resolution applies to its answering version and descendants; it does not legalize an older driver. Shared semantic issues follow actual dependencies, not checker names.\n\nREPAIR Distinguish review aspect from challenged component. F4 repairs unreached experiment prerequisites. Ordinary technical repair preserves shared property descriptions, events, identities, predicates and legality; it needs no preliminary review or encoding refactor unless an actual dispute/change requires one. Tool, parser and framework failures are not semantic feedback. Executed harness changes require a new artifact, fresh execution and current correspondence. Driver/configuration/initialization repairs name repair_issue_ids, preserve the requirement and oracle, and replace only sourced current premises. Changed observation/oracle encoding uses explicit correction; changed normative meaning/applicability uses F2, and proposition-preserving dependency expansion uses F3. Resolve against the actual changed component, never an unrelated edit. If additional source evidence answers the issue without changing inputs, resolve on that executed version instead of manufacturing a harness rewrite. Remaining issues and the current version's missing correspondence stay visible independently.\nEXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n\nCOMPLETION Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. Check a wait's return or record actual attainment when it establishes a necessary premise; when waiting is the investigated behavior, requiring success would discard the failure history. Sleep establishes elapsed time, not synchronization, completion or a coherent snapshot; a printed readiness flag is not a prerequisite witness. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability from independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output. Distinct formal scenarios need their actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by observed results or missing premises after execution. Role readiness does not imply that earlier work drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve caller/transport duties; prefer one policy-selected delivery path and record the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish receipt, per-message-type queueing and dispatch; preserve the replaced layer's ordering without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. A repeatable suffix must account for behavior-determining state, schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal business fields do not close execution. A rescue stimulus may itself be required caller work.\n\nCORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed. It is not the first prerequisite by array order. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisite events only; monitors select independent result events. ObservableProperty.identity_fields declares the stable operation identity once, using fields present at the relevant observation points. Do not repeat a result as a prerequisite or duplicate each identity equality as a Comparison. Reference conditions declare necessary predecessor relationships; unrelated prerequisites have no implicit list order. Assertions may refer to any declared prerequisite alias that actually precedes the result. Missing identity/reference fields or nonunique associations remain unknown. Independent applicability is checked before requiring unrelated history. Alias-dependent applicability follows correlation. Each operation is matched separately. A complete violating witness survives missing results in demonstrably independent operations, while coverage remains partial. Same-witness ambiguity and potentially global parse loss still block attribution. Use independent identity, not the compared value, to associate an input and output. A context expected to change cannot also be an equality filter. More complex histories need actual correlated prerequisites and results; unsupported general temporal expressions remain a stated limitation.\n\nMEANING Distinguish the written obligation, the proposition encoded by applicability/trigger/antecedent/assertion, and what this execution actually compared. Type, count or numeric-position equality may be necessary without establishing content or identity equality. Record comparisons and scope limits separately. Identify live object, copy, cache or caller-maintained observations, their writers and the synchronization or ownership boundary supporting the read; multiple fields must represent the state the proposition needs. Include ownership of injection flags, counters and sampling itself. An export discrepancy need not mean active protocol state changed. Match observation to the claim: stopping may change the behavior; neither shutdown sampling, locks, public APIs, dual reads nor race detection are universally required. Challenge specific unreliable reads, not all concurrent checks. Keep unresolved contracts, counterevidence, input legality and observation differences explicit; CheckRun owns execution status. An implementation/requirement discrepancy is the subject, not a conflict between requirement sources. Real contradictions remain conflicts.\n\nCONFIRMATION Reconstruct decisive relationships from the fixed test, actual constructors/producers and raw events; the plan's legality account is a claim to verify. Check prepared state, substituted calls and identity/context/generation across stages; constructible inputs or isolated fragments do not establish one legal history. Preserve relevant queues, callbacks, lock ownership and caller/transport duties. For waiting, missing replies or retained resources, trace waiter, result/cancel/close producer, normal shutdown entry and the observation's shutdown phase. Verify which owner/caller actually performs cleanup: no local timeout does not prove permanent waiting, and an available Close method does not prove it ran. A direct post-stop handler call differs from production dispatch still reaching it. Sourced local interface or exit duties need no whole-deployment proof. Review oracle, parsing, reached premises and completion together. Use rationale, source_ids, counterevidence, challenged_components and exact ReviewIssues for discrepancies; choose driver repair, encoding or F2/F3 by what changes, never weaken the written responsibility to rescue confirmation. Incompatible inputs are attribution gaps. Local functions, injectable storage, bounded initialization and substitute schedules remain valid when the sourced proposition permits them. Preserve measurements while correspondence is pending; complete local counterexamples survive independent wider-history or endpoint limits. New source counterevidence may challenge prior confirmation; an unobserved wider endpoint remains a limit.\nNECESSITY For S implies E, compare S when independently established E is false, or use equivalent supported implication encoding; never strengthen to S equals E or filter the result through applicability. In a complete implication comparison, observed S=false retains holds but supports only that S did not occur here, not E or universal consistency; S=true actually tests E. Missing results, identity or prerequisites are not observed falsity and cannot supply holds. Do not require every conditional branch to execute before confirming a complete local counterexample, or infer eventual success from a permitted pending control.\npackage dlog\n\nimport (\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"os\"\n)\n\nvar DLOG = false\n\nfunc Printf(format string, v ...any) {\n\tif DLOG {\n\t\tlog.Printf(format, v...)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc Println(v ...any) {\n\tif DLOG {\n\t\tlog.Println(v...)\n\t}\n}\n\ntype Logger struct {\n\tlogger  *log.Logger\n\tverbose bool\n}\n\nfunc New(logPath string, verbose bool) *Logger {\n\tlogF := os.Stdout\n\tif logPath != \"\" {\n\t\tvar err error\n\t\tlogF, err = os.OpenFile(logPath, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, 0644)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tlog.Fatal(\"Can't open log file:\", logPath)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn &Logger{\n\t\tlogger:  log.New(logF, \"\", log.LstdFlags),\n\t\tverbose: verbose,\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *Logger) Println(v ...any) {\n\tif l == nil {\n\t\tlog.Println(v...)\n\t}\n\tif l.verbose {\n\t\tl.logger.Println(v...)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *Logger) Printf(format string, v ...any) {\n\tif l == nil {\n\t\tlog.Printf(format, v...)\n\t}\n\tif l.verbose {\n\t\tl.logger.Printf(format, v...)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *Logger) Fatal(v ...any) {\n\tif l == nil {\n\t\tlog.Fatal(v...)\n\t}\n\tif l.verbose {\n\t\tl.logger.Fatal(v...)\n\t}\n}\npackage replica\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"encoding/binary\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"math\"\n\t\"net\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/config\"\n\t\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/dlog\"\n\t\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/replica/defs\"\n\tfastrpc \"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/rpc\"\n\t\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/state\"\n)\n\ntype Replica struct {\n\t*dlog.Logger\n\n\tM     sync.Mutex\n\tN     int\n\tF     int\n\tId    int32\n\tAlias string\n\n\tPeerAddrList       []string\n\tPeers              []net.Conn\n\tPeerReaders        []*bufio.Reader\n\tPeerWriters        []*bufio.Writer\n\tClientWriters      map[int32]*bufio.Writer\n\tConfig             *config.Config\n\tAlive              []bool\n\tPreferredPeerOrder []int32\n\n\tState       *state.State\n\tRPC         *fastrpc.Table\n\tStableStore *os.File\n\tStats       *defs.Stats\n\tShutdown    bool\n\tListener    net.Listener\n\tProposeChan chan *defs.GPropose\n\tBeaconChan  chan *defs.GBeacon\n\n\tThrifty bool\n\tExec    bool\n\tLRead   bool\n\tDreply  bool\n\tBeacon  bool\n\tDurable bool\n\n\tEwma      []float64\n\tLatencies []int64\n\n\tDt *defs.LatencyTable\n}\n\nfunc New(alias string, id, f int, addrs []string, thrifty, exec, lread bool, config *config.Config, l *dlog.Logger) *Replica {\npackage rpc\n\nimport \"io\"\n\ntype Serializable interface {\n\tMarshal(io.Writer)\n\tUnmarshal(io.Reader) error\n\tNew() Serializable\n}\n\ntype Pair struct {\n\tObj  Serializable\n\tChan chan Serializable\n}\n\ntype Table struct {\n\tid    uint8\n\tpairs map[uint8]Pair\n}\n\nfunc NewTable() *Table {\n\treturn &Table{\n\t\tid:    0,\n\t\tpairs: make(map[uint8]Pair),\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc NewTableId(id uint8) *Table {\n\treturn &Table{\n\t\tid:    id,\n\t\tpairs: make(map[uint8]Pair),\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (t *Table) Register(obj Serializable, notify chan Serializable) uint8 {\n\tid := t.id\n\tt.id++\n\tt.pairs[id] = Pair{\n\t\tObj:  obj,\n\t\tChan: notify,\n\t}\n\treturn id\n}\n\nfunc (t *Table) Get(id uint8) (Pair, bool) {\n\tp, exists := t.pairs[id]\n\treturn p, exists\n}\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"const\": \"explore\",\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Question\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"harness_path\": {\n      \"title\": \"Harness Path\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"execution_package\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Optional single local Go package or Rust crate directory, with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package\",\n      \"title\": \"Execution Package\"\n    },\n    \"files\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Files\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"question\",\n    \"harness_path\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ExploreSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > explore_accept_recovery_test.go <<'GO'\npackage epaxos\n\nimport (\n \\\"bufio\\\"\n \\\"bytes\\\"\n \\\"encoding/json\\\"\n \\\"fmt\\\"\n \\\"testing\\\"\n\n \\\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/dlog\\\"\n \\\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/replica\\\"\n \\\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/replica/defs\\\"\n fastrpc \\\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/rpc\\\"\n \\\"github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos/state\\\"\n)\n\ntype assuranceEnvelope struct { from,to int; msg fastrpc.Serializable }\ntype assuranceNet struct { t *testing.T; nodes []*Replica; wire [][]*bytes.Buffer; queue []assuranceEnvelope; step int }\nfunc assuranceEvent(kind string, fields map[string]any) { fields[\\\"kind\\\"]=kind; b,err:=json.Marshal(fields); if err\"'!=nil {panic(err)}; fmt.Println(\"CA_EVENT \"+string(b)) }\nfunc assuranceNewNet(t *testing.T) *assuranceNet {\n const n=5\n net:=&assuranceNet{t:t,nodes:make([]*Replica,n),wire:make([][]*bytes.Buffer,n)}\n for id:=0;id<n;id++ {\n  base:=&replica.Replica{Logger:dlog.New(\"\",false),N:n,F:2,Id:int32(id),Thrifty:true,Dreply:true,State:state.InitState(),Stats:&defs.Stats{M:make(map[string]int)},Alive:make([]bool,n),PreferredPeerOrder:make([]int32,n),PeerWriters:make([]*bufio.Writer,n),ProposeChan:make(chan *defs.GPropose,16),RPC:fastrpc.NewTableId(defs.RPC_TABLE)}\n  r:=&Replica{Replica:base,InstanceSpace:make([][]*Instance,n),crtInstance:make([]int32,n),CommittedUpTo:make([]int32,n),ExecedUpTo:make([]int32,n),conflicts:make([]map[state.Key]*InstPair,n),maxSeqPerKey:make(map[state.Key]int32),maxRecvBallot:-1,latestCPInstance:-1,instancesToRecover:make(chan *instanceId,16)}\n  net.nodes[id]=r;net.wire[id]=make([]*bytes.Buffer,n)\n  for q:=0;q<n;q++ { r.InstanceSpace[q]=make([]*Instance,16);r.crtInstance[q]=-1;r.CommittedUpTo[q]=-1;r.ExecedUpTo[q]=-1;r.conflicts[q]=make(map[state.Key]*InstPair);r.Alive[q]=true;r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]=int32((id+1+q)%n);net.wire[id][q]=new(bytes.Buffer);r.PeerWriters[q]=bufio.NewWriter(net.wire[id][q]) }\n  r.prepareRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(Prepare),nil);r.prepareReplyRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(PrepareReply),nil);r.preAcceptRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(PreAccept),nil);r.preAcceptReplyRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(PreAcceptReply),nil);r.acceptRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(Accept),nil);r.acceptReplyRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(AcceptReply),nil);r.commitRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(Commit),nil);r.tryPreAcceptRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(TryPreAccept),nil);r.tryPreAcceptReplyRPC=base.RPC.Register(new(TryPreAcceptReply),nil)\n }\n return net\n}\nfunc (n *assuranceNet) collect() {\n for from,row:=range n.wire { for to,b:=range row {for b.Len()>0 {code,err:=b.ReadByte();if err!=nil{n.t.Fatal(err)};pair,ok:=n.nodes[to].RPC.Get(code);if !ok{n.t.Fatal(\"unknown RPC\",code)};msg:=pair.Obj.New();if err:=msg.Unmarshal(b);err!=nil{n.t.Fatal(err)};n.queue=append(n.queue,assuranceEnvelope{from,to,msg});assuranceEvent(\"send\",map[string]any{\"from\":from,\"to\":to,\"type\":fmt.Sprintf(\"%T\",msg),\"message\":msg})}} }\n}\nfunc (n *assuranceNet) deliver(from,to int,typ string, origin,slot int32) {\n n.t.Helper()\n for i,e:=range n.queue {if e.from!=from||e.to!=to||fmt.Sprintf(\"%T\",e.msg)!=typ {continue};var r,s int32\n  switch m:=e.msg.(type){case *PreAccept:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *PreAcceptReply:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *Accept:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *AcceptReply:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *Prepare:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *PrepareReply:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;case *Commit:r,s=m.Replica,m.Instance;default:n.t.Fatal(\"unsupported dispatch\")}\n  if r!=origin||s!=slot{continue};n.queue=append(n.queue[:i],n.queue[i+1:]...);n.step++;assuranceEvent(\"dispatch\",map[string]any{\"step\":n.step,\"from\":from,\"to\":to,\"type\":typ,\"message\":e.msg})\n  target:=n.nodes[to];switch m:=e.msg.(type){case *PreAccept:target.handlePreAccept(m);case *PreAcceptReply:target.handlePreAcceptReply(m);case *Accept:target.handleAccept(m);case *AcceptReply:target.handleAcceptReply(m);case *Prepare:target.handlePrepare(m);case *PrepareReply:target.handlePrepareReply(m);case *Commit:target.handleCommit(m)};n.collect();return\n };n.t.Fatalf(\"missing %s %d->%d for %d.%d\",typ,from,to,origin,slot)\n}\nfunc (n *assuranceNet) snapshot(label string,id int,origin,slot int32) {\n inst:=n.nodes[id].InstanceSpace[origin][slot];if inst==nil{assuranceEvent(label,map[string]any{\"observer\":id,\"replica\":origin,\"instance\":slot,\"present\":false});return}\n assuranceEvent(label,map[string]any{\"observer\":id,\"replica\":origin,\"instance\":slot,\"present\":true,\"status\":inst.Status,\"ballot\":inst.bal,\"value_ballot\":inst.vbal,\"commands\":inst.Cmds,\"seq\":inst.Seq,\"deps\":inst.Deps})\n}\nfunc TestAssuranceExploreAcceptRecovery(t *testing.T) {\n n:=assuranceNewNet(t)\n // Bounded constructor-equivalent storage, serial handlers and captured real wire bytes.\n // No application executor, client reply waiter, timers or network goroutines run.\n // The schedule retains rather than drains undelivered messages.\n for _,id:=range []int{1,0} {r:=n.nodes[id];r.handlePropose(&defs.GPropose{Propose:&defs.Propose{Command:state.Command{Op:state.PUT,K:10,V:state.Value{byte(id+1)}}}});n.collect()}\n n.deliver(0,1,\"*epaxos.PreAccept\",0,0);n.deliver(0,2,\"*epaxos.PreAccept\",0,0)\n n.deliver(1,0,\"*epaxos.PreAcceptReply\",0,0);n.deliver(2,0,\"*epaxos.PreAcceptReply\",0,0)\n n.snapshot(\"coordinator_after_preaccept\",0,0,0)\n for _,id:=range []int{1,2} {n.deliver(0,id,\"*epaxos.Accept\",0,0);n.snapshot(\"follower_after_accept\",id,0,0)}\n n.deliver(1,0,\"*epaxos.AcceptReply\",0,0);n.deliver(2,0,\"*epaxos.AcceptReply\",0,0)\n n.snapshot(\"original_coordinator_decision\",0,0,0)\n // Replica 0 stops participating after producing Commit; its messages remain in flight.\n for _,r:=range n.nodes {r.Alive[0]=false}\n assuranceEvent(\"fault_policy\",map[string]any{\"failed_replica\":0,\"future_dispatch_to_or_from_failed\":false,\"pending_messages\":len(n.queue)})\n // Direct recovery entry is exploratory: unseen-slot admission by the scanner is not assumed.\n n.nodes[3].startRecoveryForInstance(0,0);n.collect();n.snapshot(\"recoverer_after_start\",3,0,0)\n n.deliver(3,1,\"*epaxos.Prepare\",0,0);n.deliver(3,2,\"*epaxos.Prepare\",0,0)\n n.deliver(1,3,\"*epaxos.PrepareReply\",0,0);n.deliver(2,3,\"*epaxos.PrepareReply\",0,0)\n n.snapshot(\"recoverer_after_prepare\",3,0,0)\n for _,id:=range []int{4,1}{n.deliver(3,id,\"*epaxos.PreAccept\",0,0)}\n for _,id:=range []int{4,1}{n.deliver(id,3,\"*epaxos.PreAcceptReply\",0,0)}\n for _,id:=range []int{4,1}{n.deliver(3,id,\"*epaxos.Accept\",0,0)}\n for _,id:=range []int{4,1}{n.deliver(id,3,\"*epaxos.AcceptReply\",0,0)}\n n.snapshot(\"recovery_coordinator_decision\",3,0,0)\n assuranceEvent(\"exploration_complete\",map[string]any{\"pending_messages\":len(n.queue),\"dispatch_count\":n.step})\n}\nGO\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\ns=dict(action='explore',rationale='Construct a real-wire slow-path prefix and inspect follower status exported to recovery. An empty recoverer also tests the independent self-vbal selection mechanism. Direct unseen-slot recovery entry remains conditional exploration, not a legal whole-cluster witness or property evidence.',question='After a coordinator receives two Accept acknowledgements in N=5 and stops before Commit delivery, what support do followers export, and what does recovery select when its local slot was absent? Does retained vbal/attribute data overcome the unchanged status, or does another producer erase that protection?',harness_path='explore_accept_recovery_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['67ded68bdd3b49d7ba28b333d9eb0caf','M-accept','M-recovery','M-dispatch','M-listener'],answered='Source tracing confirms AcceptReply carries only identity and current ballot, while PrepareReply carries the unchanged follower status. Recovery self-reply is generated after assigning the new attempt to inst.vbal, introducing an independent selection premise. A serialized handler driver can capture real wire bytes and retain in-flight messages without inventing reply contents.',remaining=['Determine actual output under the constructed conditional recovery entry.','An unseen slot must become scanner-eligible through sourced history before this can be a production recovery witness.','A later formal requirement must distinguish follower support retention from self-reply value-ballot selection.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Execution can distinguish which producer/consumer mechanism determines the selected tuple; this exploration does not settle the Candidate.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-explore.json','w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission-explore.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
